      "text": "1. We know that $\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} ma + nb \\\\ pa + qb \\end{pmatrix}$,\nfor any values of $m$, $n$, $p$, and $q$.\n2. So, we can write the following equations: $\\begin{cases} ma + nb = 6 \\\\ pa + qb = 21 \\end{cases}$, $\\begin{cases} ma + nb = 3 \\\\ pa + qb = -17 \\end{cases}$.\n3. We can solve these two equations simultaneously to find the values of $m$ and $p$.\n4. Subtract the second equation from the first equation to eliminate $b$: $\\begin{cases} ma + nb = 6 - a \\\\ pa + qb = 21 - b \\end{cases}$.\n5. Then, we have the following system of equations: $\\begin{cases} ax + by = 2a + b + 18 \\\\ ax + by = 0 \\\\ bx + ay = 6 - a \\\\ by + ax = 49 - b \\end{cases}$.\n6. Solving this system of equations gives us $m = 2$ and $p = 5$.\n7. Therefore, $\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\end{pmatrix}$.\n\n$$\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 \\end{pmatrix}}$$",
