      "text": "Given the equations:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nand \n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\nwe aim to find the matrix $\\mathbf{M}$. Let \n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nWe are given:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis translates into the system:\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFrom this we get two equations:\n\\[\n3a = 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 3c = 21\n\\]\n\nSolving these:\n\\[\na = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c = 7\n\\]\n\nNext, we consider:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThis translates into the system:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a - b \\\\ c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFrom this we get two equations:\n\\[\na - b = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c + 5d = -17\n\\]\n\nWe have already established:\n\\[\na = 2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad c = 7\n\\]\n\nUsing \\(a = 2\\) in \\(a - b = 3\\):\n\\[\n2 - b = 3 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad b = -1\n\\]\n\nWe use \\(a = 2\\) in \\(c + 5d = -17\\):\n\\[\n7 + 5d = -17 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 5d = -24 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad d = -\\frac{24}{5}\n\\]\n\nPutting all this together, \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -\\frac{24}{5} \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -\\frac{24}{5} \\end{pmatrix}}\\).",
