      "text": "Given the conditions for the matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\),\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\nwe introduce \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) in general form as:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirstly, applying the first equation to \\(\\mathbf{M}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} \n\\]\n\nresults in:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 3a \\\\ 3c \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 6 \\\\ 21 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFrom this system of equations, we get:\n\n\\[\n3a = 6 \\implies a = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n3c = 21 \\implies c = 7\n\\]\n\nNext, applying the second equation to \\(\\mathbf{M}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix} \n\\]\n\nresulting in:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -a + 5b \\\\ -c + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the initial values \\(a = 2\\) and \\(c = 7\\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -2 + 5b \\\\ -7 + 5d \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ -17 \\end{pmatrix} \n\\]\n\nWe now solve for \\(b\\) and \\(d\\) separately. For \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n-2 + 5b = 3 \\implies 5b = 5 \\implies b = 1\n\\]\n\nFor \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\n-7 + 5d = -17 \\implies 5d = -10 \\implies d = -2\n\\]\n\nThus, the \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrix \\(\\mathbf{M}\\) that satisfies the given conditions is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFinally, putting the final answer in \\boxed{} form is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -2 \\end{pmatrix}}\n\\]",
